{"name":"Cardboard","hex":"#c19a6c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cardboard","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A wood-based material resembling heavy paper, used in the manufacture of boxes, cartons and signs.","Corrugated cardboard."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of or resembling cardboard.","Flat or flavorless."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cardboard"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cardboard","blocks":[{"text":"Cardboard is a generic term for heavy paper-based products ranging from a thick paper known as paperboard to corrugated fiberboard."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/57_Cardboard_stacked_for_recycling_pick_up_in_Kuala_Lumpur%2C_Malaysia_-_free_photo_with_attribution_%28Creative_Commons%29.jpg/330px-57_Cardboard_stacked_for_recycling_pick_up_in_Kuala_Lumpur%2C_Malaysia_-_free_photo_with_attribution_%28Creative_Commons%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cardboard"},{"title":"Cardboard (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Cardboard is a 2025 British animated short film written and directed by J.P. Vine and produced by Locksmith Animation, DNEG Animation and Ritzy Animation. The short film, which is about a family of homeless pigs, was selected in various festivals, including the Annecy International Animation Film Festival, the LA Shorts International Film Festival, the BFI London Film Festival, the Flickers Rhode Island International Film Festival and the Animation Is Film Festival. Cardboard was shortlisted for Best Animated Short Film at the 98th Academy Awards and was also nominated for Best Animated Short Subject at the 53rd Annie Awards in 2026."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/88/Cardboard_Film_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cardboard_(film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://